[(flags. In the basic example on the left, we have the)]
[('-resize' flag in the read message that resizes the)]
[(array to the file size. See more about flags and)]
[(advanced examples in the subpatch below.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 580 553 [
[(Also note: Loading a soundfile into an array might be)]
[(useful for more flexible playing strategies with table)]
[(reading objects in the 'see also' section below. For a)]
[(simpler alternative that streams a soundfile directly)]
[(from your hard drive, see [readsf~].)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 581 475 [
[(When loading or writing a file, the left outlet)]
[(outputs the file's number of samples. If you're)]
[(loading a file that is bigger than the array size, the)]
[(number or samples gets clipped to the array size \050you)]
[(probably want to use the -resize flag in this case to)]
[(automatically resize the array size to the file size\051.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 581 381 [
[(The right outlet sends information as a list, namely:)]
[(Sample Rate, Header Size, Number of Channels, Bytes)]
[(per Sample and Endianness: "b" \050for "big"\051 or "l" \050for)]
[("little"\051.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
0 581 316 [
[(Important: The number of channels is limited to 64 for)]
[(both reading and writing.)]
] 14 -0 0 0 false DrawText
grestore
gsave
/Menlo findfont 12 scalefont ISOEncode setfont
0.000 0.000 0.000 setrgbcolor AdjustColor
